  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Given below are two statements :</p><p>Statement I: <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>Ni</mi><msub><mfenced><mi>CN</mi></mfenced><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math> is square planar and diamagnetic complex, with&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>dsp</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;hybridization for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Ni</mi></math> but <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>Ni</mi><msub><mfenced><mi>CO</mi></mfenced><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math> is tetrahedral, paramagnetic and with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>sp</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math> hybridication&nbsp;for&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Ni</mi></math>.</p><p>Statement II : <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><msub><mi>NiCl</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>Ni</mi><msub><mfenced><mi>CO</mi></mfenced><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math> both have same d-electron configuration, have same geometry and are paramagnetic.</p><p>In light the above statements, choose the correct answer form the options given below</p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are true.",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Statement I is correct but statement II is false.",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Statement I is incorrect but statement II is true.",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are false.",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>Ni</mi><msub><mfenced><mi>CN</mi></mfenced><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>8</mn></msup></math> configuration, SFL, sq. planar splitting <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><msup><mi>dsp</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfenced></math>, diamagnetic.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>Ni</mi><msub><mfenced><mi>CO</mi></mfenced><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>10</mn></msup></math> config (after excitation), SFL, tetrahedral splitting <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><msup><mi>sp</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mfenced></math>, diamagnetic.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><msub><mi>NiCl</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>8</mn></msup></math> config, WFL, tetrahedral splitting <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><msup><mi>sp</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mfenced></math>, paramagnetic(<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;unpaired <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mo>-</mo></msup></math>).</p><p>Electronic configuration of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Ni</mi></math>&nbsp;atom in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Ni</mi><msub><mfenced><mi>CO</mi></mfenced><mn>4</mn></msub></math></p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\st0172_8af604f9a0eb.png\" style=\"width: 550px; height: 568px;\" /></p>"
  }
